<p>Cuba began releasing prisoners on April 3 after announcing pardons for 2,010 inmates. Journalists at Havana&#x27;s La Lima penitentiary saw emotional reunions as freed prisoners left with release papers and embraced waiting relatives. Cuban authorities described the move as a &quot;humanitarian and sovereign gesture&quot; tied to Holy Week, even as the island faced one of the strongest US pressure campaigns in decades. The move also came days after President Trump eased a de facto oil blockade by allowing a Russian tanker to deliver crude to fuel-starved Cuba, while Washington kept pressing for political change and the release of political prisoners. Rights groups and US officials welcomed clarity on the scale of the amnesty, but one important question remains unanswered: Havana has not published a list of those pardoned, so it is still unclear whether political detainees are among them.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/wWdrCUUnfqeuqgyCKG8LXgNsOR5SgS8Bltvb7uI67QZxo-gG1KR0XeOoimxwX0q_bzimS09y1NANDDVzJqBUJNDaPavFWfd4BcTxTG7r0UA12vshDQ-VNgFoTQnFSjeBq_7YhSAoHeWONhUwBR0TjizsogTvOWo0r7rNW0-pCAIqWLseV_rk9gvcg92YcCV9rbwPMVWEfnPJJP-Qy36oWD9u7-l3rWCd8fXcpWJnr2Qn7LdMFwI3Is9RXV_YwC05AcyCyrN5yUbAYbPF5g' alt='Emilio Alejandro Leyva, a pardoned prisoner, hugs his mother Katia Arias after his release from La Lima penitentiary in Cuba on Friday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Second release: This is Cuba&#x27;s second prisoner release in less than a month, highlighting a rapid series of amnesty moves during a period of economic strain and diplomatic pressure.</li><li>No public list: Authorities did not publish the names of those pardoned, making independent verification difficult and leaving open how many, if any, were jailed for political reasons.</li><li>Family scenes: More than 20 inmates were seen leaving La Lima penitentiary in east Havana on Friday, many crying and hugging relatives who had waited outside all morning.</li><li>US demand: Releasing political prisoners has long been a central US demand in dealings with Cuba, giving this amnesty significance beyond the immediate humanitarian gesture.</li></ul><blockquote>Thank you for this opportunity that they gave us. - Albis Gainza</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cuban government: Havana presented the pardon as a &quot;humanitarian and sovereign gesture&quot; to mark Holy Week and did not publicly tie it to talks with the United States. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/03/cuba-to-release-pardon-prisoners-us-fuel-blockade'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Human rights groups: Rights advocates pressed for clarity on whether detainees from past anti-government protests were included, saying the lack of a published list leaves key accountability questions unresolved. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-cuba-freed-prisoners-human-rights-havana-releases/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Andres Pertierra, University of Wisconsin historian: He said the timing fits a familiar pattern in US-Cuba relations, arguing that official denials of negotiation links often accompany moves that clearly line up with diplomatic bargaining. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988358/cuba-begins-prisoner-release-after-mass-pardon'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Freed prisoners and families: The first releases brought emotional scenes outside the prison, with relatives celebrating reunions and some former inmates publicly hoping the process would continue. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/3/cuba-releases-over-2000-prisoners-amid-mounting-us-pressure'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/03/cuba-to-release-pardon-prisoners-us-fuel-blockade'>Cuba begins to free more than 2,000 prisoners as US eases fuel blockade</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/cuba-begins-releasing-prisoners-under-scrutiny-of-rights-groups-u-s-govt'>Cuba begins releasing prisoners under scrutiny of rights groups, U.S. govt</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/cuba-pardons-2010-people-us-pressures-islands-government-131673655'>Cuba pardons 2,010 people as the U.S. pressures the island&#x27;s government</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988358/cuba-begins-prisoner-release-after-mass-pardon'>Cuba begins prisoner release after mass pardon</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/03/cuban-prisoners-freed-after-mass-pardon_6752091_4.html'>Cuban prisoners freed after mass pardon</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-cuba-freed-prisoners-human-rights-havana-releases/'>As freed Cuban prisoners celebrate, human rights groups demand clarity on detained protesters</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy3r3w4zl8o'>Cuba begins releasing more than 2,000 prisoners as US pressure mounts</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cuba-releases-prisoners-trump-administration-pressure-on-island-oil-russia/'>Cuba says it released over 2,000 prisoners as White House heaps pressure on island</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/3/cuba-releases-over-2000-prisoners-amid-mounting-us-pressure'>Cuba releases over 2,000 prisoners amid mounting US pressure</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>